    fullDescription: "33 Rue Majorelle is one of Marrakech's best-loved concept stores and the ideal shopping stop to pair with a visit to the neighbouring Jardin Majorelle and Yves Saint Laurent Museum in the new town. Housed in a chic, airy space, it was created to showcase the work of contemporary Moroccan designers and artisans under one beautiful roof, and it now stocks pieces from well over a hundred of them, all thoughtfully curated and attractively displayed. The result is a treasure trove of stylish, high-quality and often unique goods that celebrate modern Moroccan design and craft: fashion and accessories, jewellery, babouches and bags, ceramics and homeware, textiles and rugs, natural beauty products, art, books and beautifully packaged gifts and edibles. Unlike the souks, everything carries a fixed price, clearly marked, so there is no haggling and no pressure — you can browse at leisure, knowing you are paying a fair, transparent rate for pieces whose provenance and quality are assured. Prices sit in the mid-to-upper range, reflecting the design credentials and the support the shop provides to local makers, but for many visitors that is a worthwhile trade for the ease, the curation and the confidence that they are buying genuinely good, ethically produced Moroccan design rather than mass-market souvenirs. There is a pleasant café attached for a break. It is the perfect place to find special gifts and keepsakes, to discover contemporary Moroccan creativity, and to shop stress-free after (or before) tackling the more chaotic bargaining of the medina souks. For quality, style and peace of mind, 33 Rue Majorelle is hard to beat.",
