    fullDescription: "Marrakech Menara Airport (RAK) is a modern, well-connected international airport located remarkably close to the city — just about six kilometres south-west of the centre, or roughly a fifteen-minute drive to the medina — which makes arriving and departing refreshingly quick and easy compared with many destinations. It handles a wide range of scheduled and low-cost flights from across Europe and beyond, along with growing intercontinental connections. Getting into town is straightforward, with a few options at different price points. The most common is a petit taxi (the beige airport taxis): these are metered by law, but drivers at the airport are notorious for trying to negotiate an inflated flat fare with arriving tourists, so either firmly insist they run the meter or agree a fair price before getting in — a fair rate to the medina or Gueliz is somewhere around 70–100 MAD, a little more at night when tariffs rise. For the budget-conscious, the public airport bus (line 19) runs a convenient loop from the airport to Jemaa el-Fnaa and on through the new town roughly every half-hour for around 30 MAD (with a return ticket valid for a couple of weeks), taking a bit longer but costing a fraction of a taxi. The most hassle-free option, particularly for first-time visitors, families or those arriving late, is to pre-book a private transfer through your riad or an online service: a driver meets you with a name board, the price is fixed in advance, and — invaluably — they will guide you the last stretch on foot to your riad through the car-free medina lanes, which can otherwise be bewildering with luggage. Whichever you choose, the short distance means you will be settling into the city in no time.",
